<p>This crystal <font color=3D"#FF0000"><strong>is incompatible </strong></=
font>with the STM32H743 MCU.</p>
<p>Tip: According to the gain margin formula, it is better to select a lowe=
r rated frequency for the crystal to reduce the value <em>gm crit</em> as m=
uch as possible, thereby increasing the gain margin.</p>
<p>Attached at the end of the article, you will find an <font color=3D"#000=
0FF"><em>STM32 Crystal Calculator.xlsx</em></font> file that can help you t=
o calculate the gain margin and quickly find a suitable crystal.</p>
<h2 id=3D"toc-hId--632922784">4. Calculation of the external load capacitor=
s value</h2>
<p>After finding the suitable crystal, it is time to calculate the external=
 load capacitors value of C<sub>L1&nbsp;</sub>and C<sub>L2</sub>. The formu=
la is as the following:&nbsp;<span class=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrappe=
r lia-image-align-center" image-alt=3D"mALLEm_12-1741349792086.png" style=
=3D"width: 263px;"><span class=3D"lia-message-image-wrapper"><img src=3D"ht=
tps://community.st.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/103026i417039EDD02F157C=
/image-dimensions/263x67/is-moderation-mode/true?v=3Dv2" width=3D"263" heig=
ht=3D"67" role=3D"button" title=3D"mALLEm_12-1741349792086.png" alt=3D"mALL=
Em_12-1741349792086.png" li-image-url=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/image/=
serverpage/image-id/103026i417039EDD02F157C?v=3Dv2" li-image-display-id=3D"=
'103026i417039EDD02F157C'" li-message-uid=3D"'780236'" li-messages-message-=
image=3D"true" li-bindable=3D"" class=3D"lia-media-image" tabindex=3D"0" li=
-bypass-lightbox-when-linked=3D"true" li-use-hover-links=3D"false" li-compi=
led=3D"true"><!----></span></span></p>
<p>In general, these two capacitors (C<sub>L1&nbsp;</sub>and C<sub>L2</sub>=
) are selected with the same capacitance: C<sub>L1&nbsp;</sub>=3D C<sub>L2<=
/sub>, which results in:</p>
<p><span class=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-center" =
image-alt=3D"mALLEm_0-1743153284389.png" style=3D"width: 274px;"><span clas=
s=3D"lia-message-image-wrapper"><img src=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/ima=
ge/serverpage/image-id/104947i860169061CBA56E1/image-dimensions/274x68/is-m=
oderation-mode/true?v=3Dv2" width=3D"274" height=3D"68" role=3D"button" tit=
le=3D"mALLEm_0-1743153284389.png" alt=3D"mALLEm_0-1743153284389.png" li-ima=
ge-url=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/104947i8601=
69061CBA56E1?v=3Dv2" li-image-display-id=3D"'104947i860169061CBA56E1'" li-m=
essage-uid=3D"'780236'" li-messages-message-image=3D"true" li-bindable=3D""=
 class=3D"lia-media-image" tabindex=3D"0" li-bypass-lightbox-when-linked=3D=
"true" li-use-hover-links=3D"false" li-compiled=3D"true"><!----></span></sp=
an></p>
<p class=3D"lia-align-center">After transforming the equation, the result i=
s:</p>
<p><span class=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-center" =
image-alt=3D"mALLEm_1-1743153327007.png" style=3D"width: 363px;"><span clas=
s=3D"lia-message-image-wrapper"><img src=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/ima=
ge/serverpage/image-id/104948i58FB42D686BD9F25/image-dimensions/363x41/is-m=
oderation-mode/true?v=3Dv2" width=3D"363" height=3D"41" role=3D"button" tit=
le=3D"mALLEm_1-1743153327007.png" alt=3D"mALLEm_1-1743153327007.png" li-ima=
ge-url=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/104948i58FB=
42D686BD9F25?v=3Dv2" li-image-display-id=3D"'104948i58FB42D686BD9F25'" li-m=
essage-uid=3D"'780236'" li-messages-message-image=3D"true" li-bindable=3D""=
 class=3D"lia-media-image" tabindex=3D"0" li-bypass-lightbox-when-linked=3D=
"true" li-use-hover-links=3D"false" li-compiled=3D"true"><!----></span></sp=
an></p>
<p>C<sub>s</sub> (stray capacitance) is an estimation of the sum of the MCU=
 pins and the parasitic capacitance of the PCB. Experience has shown that t=
he value is between 2...3 pF.</p>
<p>Note that in most of STM32 datasheets, C<sub>IO</sub> is provided as 5 p=
F and this is the worst case typical condition of 5 pF <u>which is generic =
to all I/Os</u>.</p>
<p>Where:</p>
<ul>
<li>C<sub>IO</sub> =3D pin capacitance</li>
<li>C<sub>PCB</sub>: capacitance of the PCB.</li>
<li>C<sub>s</sub> =3D C<sub>IO</sub> + C<sub>PCB&nbsp;&nbsp;</sub>=3D 3 pF<=
/li>
</ul>
<p>If we take the example of CX3225GA8000D0PTVCC with STM32H743.</p>
<p>The crystal C<sub>L</sub>=3D 8 pF (taken from its datasheet, see figure =
4).</p>
<p>So :</p>
<ul>
<li>C<sub>s</sub> =3D 3 pF</li>
<li>C<sub>L&nbsp;</sub>=3D 8 pF</li>
</ul>
<p>The external load capacitors will have the value:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p=
>
<p><span class=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-center" =
image-alt=3D"mALLEm_2-1743153478920.png" style=3D"width: 416px;"><span clas=
s=3D"lia-message-image-wrapper"><img src=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/ima=
ge/serverpage/image-id/104949i3920A93BDE9C3BF3/image-dimensions/416x39/is-m=
oderation-mode/true?v=3Dv2" width=3D"416" height=3D"39" role=3D"button" tit=
le=3D"mALLEm_2-1743153478920.png" alt=3D"mALLEm_2-1743153478920.png" li-ima=
ge-url=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/104949i3920=
A93BDE9C3BF3?v=3Dv2" li-image-display-id=3D"'104949i3920A93BDE9C3BF3'" li-m=
essage-uid=3D"'780236'" li-messages-message-image=3D"true" li-bindable=3D""=
 class=3D"lia-media-image" tabindex=3D"0" li-bypass-lightbox-when-linked=3D=
"true" li-use-hover-links=3D"false" li-compiled=3D"true"><!----></span></sp=
an></p>
<p>This capacitance value is a standard value of capacitors on the market. =
To find capacitor standard values, please refer&nbsp;to this <a href=3D"htt=
ps://mustcalculate.com/electronics/standardvalue.php" target=3D"_self" rel=
=3D"nofollow noopener noreferrer">link</a> to get the capacitors standard v=
alue.</p>
<p class=3D"lia-align-center"><span class=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrapp=
er lia-image-align-inline" image-alt=3D"Figure 7. Standard capacitor value =
in this case is 10 pF" style=3D"width: 556px;"><span class=3D"lia-message-i=
mage-wrapper"><img src=3D"https://community.st.com/t5/image/serverpage/imag=
e-id/104950iBCB69129DAD24AA0/image-size/large/is-moderation-mode/true?v=3Dv=
2&amp;px=3D999" role=3D"button" title=3D"Figure 7.png" alt=3D"Figure 7. Sta=
ndard capacitor value in this case is 10 pF" li-image-url=3D"https://commun=
ity.st.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/104950iBCB69129DAD24AA0?v=3Dv2" li-=
image-display-id=3D"'104950iBCB69129DAD24AA0'" li-message-uid=3D"'780236'" =
li-messages-message-image=3D"true" li-bindable=3D"" class=3D"lia-media-imag=
e" tabindex=3D"0" li-bypass-lightbox-when-linked=3D"true" li-use-hover-link=
s=3D"false" li-compiled=3D"true"><!----></span><span class=3D"lia-inline-im=
age-caption">Figure 7. Standard capacitor value in this case is 10 pF</span=
></span></p>
<p>Please note that selecting a non-exact value for the calculated capacito=
r affects the frequency of the oscillator (and therefore the pullability of=
 the crystal). The more the capacitor value deviates from the calculated va=
lue, the greater the frequency deviation from the nominal frequency of the =
crystal.</p>
<p>Also note that the value of the external load capacitor in the case of <=
strong>LSE</strong> can best be determined empirically. Each time the capac=
itor changes, the RTC output frequency is measured at the MCO with a univer=
sal counter until the frequency of 32.768 kHz is reached as accurately as n=
ecessary.</p>
<p>Finally, it's interesting to note that one of the ST partners named&nbsp=
;<a href=3D"https://ecsxtal.com/design-tools/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noo=
pener nofollow noreferrer">ECS</a> provides an easy tool on this <a href=3D=
"https://ecsxtal.com/news-resources/stm32-crystal-selection-tools/" target=
=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener nofollow noreferrer">link.</a> The tool helps y=
ou to select a compatible crystal for HSE and LSE for their products based =
on the ST recommendations.</p>
<h2 id=3D"toc-hId-1109887551">5. Layout considerations</h2>
<p>Despite the best values for the capacitors and the crystal, stable opera=
tion over the entire voltage and temperature range can be difficult if a su=
itable layout has not been developed. It is therefore highly recommended to=
 work through the important notes in <a href=3D"https://www.st.com/resource=
/en/application_note/an2867-guidelines-for-oscillator-design-on-stm8afals-a=
nd-stm32-mcusmpus-stmicroelectronics.pdf#page=3D44" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer">AN2867</a>, section 7, in order to achieve the des=
ired result.</p>
<p>The following image shows figure 14 of AN2867 as an example, in which th=
e pins to which the HSE and LSE crystals that are connected, are marked wit=
h green, orange and pink circles. For better clarification, the ballout fro=
m the datasheet is also shown on the right, in which the relevant pins are =
marked.</p>
<p>What is important here is the realization of the 'trough'-shaped shieldi=
ng of both HSE crystal and LSE crystal. Each of the crystals has:</p>
<ul>
<li>its own, light blue GND 'base plate', which is separated from the other=
 GND (white dividing line).</li>
<li>An additional red GND 'wall' around the crystal and its load capacitors=
 on its assembly layer with several vias to the respective GND 'base plate'=
 of the crystal.</li>
<li>A separate GND connection of its GND 'base plate' to the nearest VSS pi=
n, possibly separate from the other VSS, as shown in <a href=3D"https://www=
.st.com/resource/en/application_note/an2867-guidelines-for-oscillator-desig=
n-on-stm8afals-and-stm32-mcusmpus-stmicroelectronics.pdf#page=3D46" target=
=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">AN2867, Figure 15</a>&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p><span class=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline" =
image-alt=3D"an2867 Figure 14 incl Ballout.png" style=3D"width: 999px;"><sp=
an class=3D"lia-message-image-wrapper"><img src=3D"https://community.st.com=
/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/106148iB1B971E3A3EA04D3/image-size/large/is-m=
oderation-mode/true?v=3Dv2&amp;px=3D999" role=3D"button" title=3D"an2867 Fi=
