						<p>Hello,</p>
<p>This article was just provided to give a newbie user how to select a sui=
table crystal on STM32. It was made as simple as possible on purpose.</p>
<p>More details and especially the calculation of Rext are explained and pr=
ovided in the <a href=3D"https://www.st.com/resource/en/application_note/an=
2867-guidelines-for-oscillator-design-on-stm8afals-and-stm32-mcusmpus-stmic=
roelectronics.pdf" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">AN2867</a>=
.&nbsp;</p>
<p>So please refer to that detailed application note.</p>
<p>PS: generally LSE doesn't need Rext. HSE, it does, in some cases.</p>
<p>Hope I answered your question.</p>
